ct  during the operator balancing sprint  workshop in barcelona spain  we regret to inform you that ubisoft  will no longer be working with you  moving forward  this includes future activations such as  the london event  taking place on october 24th we have and  always will  value the content you have created over  the years that said  we cannot and will not accept behavior  directed towards ubisoft's staff that is  disrespectful  dismissive or rude end quote shortly  after get flank put out his video  sharing his perspective on the barcelona  balancing trip rogue 9 posted another  twit longer basically disputing a lot of  the events that get flank says happened  at this point  it's become a bit of a he said he said  and the crazy thing about this situation  is that ubisoft reached out to me with a  statement long before i ever asked for  comment which to me  says that they're taking this very  seriously quote the work of content  creators is critical to the health and  integrity of our communities  and our relationship with these creators  is built on mutual respect and  professionalism  if these principles are not respected  ubisoft will take action we deem  appropriate in order to protect our  employees  partners in the wider community end  quote okay so  that wraps up the barcelona and  harassment allegations  but we're not done with everything yet  now on top of stating that the  harassment accusations are a lie  rogue 9 also makes allegations to former  siege community developers justin kruger  and craig robinson  who goes by appie online and that's how  i'll be referring to him from now on  basically these two guys were largely  responsible for working with siege  content creators whether at events  or online having a community development  team is pretty typical  they act as a buffer between the  developer and the rest of the community  while also working with content creators  and as far as siege goes  justin and craig were the go-to guys for  this type of 